{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Good.</b> Wisdom has no need of weapons of war. He already said, 'Wisdom is better than might' (Ecclesiastes 7:19) — than might of the heart — 'and it will save and protect more than weapons of war for a warrior.' Now, wisdom is found to save its owner and others with him, like the men of the small city. And the opposite of this: one sinner destroys much good, and it returns upon the ruler of fools."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:46.075986676Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}